.TH "DOCUMENTTYPE.REPLACEWITH" "3JS" "October 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DocumentType.replaceWith \- DocumentType: replaceWith() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]replaceWith()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]DocumentType\f[R] interface replaces this \f[CR]DocumentType\f[R]
in the children list of its parent with a set of \f[CR]Node\f[R] objects
or strings.
Strings are inserted as equivalent \f[CR]Text\f[R] nodes.
Nothing happens if \f[CR]parentNode\f[R] is \f[CR]null\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
replaceWith(param1)
replaceWith(param1, param2)
replaceWith(param1, param2, /* \&..., */ paramN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]param1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]paramN\f[R]
A set of \f[CR]Node\f[R] objects or strings to insert.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]HierarchyRequestError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown when the node cannot be inserted at the specified point in the
hierarchy.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using \f[CR]replaceWith()\f[R]
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] svgDt = document.implementation.createDocumentType(
  \(dqsvg:svg\(dq,
  \(dq\-//W3C//DTD SVG 1.1//EN\(dq,
  \(dqhttp://www.w3.org/Graphics/SVG/1.1/DTD/svg11.dtd\(dq,
);

document.doctype.replaceWith(svgDt);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CharacterData.replaceWith()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Element.replaceWith()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CharacterData.replaceWith()\f[R]
